# For the Common Good: "target token you control" and "tokens you control", so an opponent's token is neither a legal target nor
# helped, nor counted. Turn 1 Bot1 makes a Treasure with Gold Pan. Turn 2 Bot2 makes one too. Turn 3: Bot1 cannot cast the spell at Bot2's
# Treasure (refused), and then casts it at its own for X=0 ({G} only): no copies, but the sentence still happens, the Treasure
# gains indestructible and 1 life is gained for it (20 -> 21), not 2 for both. On turn 4 Bot2's two Disenchants: the one at Bot1's
# Treasure does not destroy it; the one at Bot2's own Treasure does (not protected, the positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Gold Pan
For the Common Good
Island x2
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Gold Pan
Disenchant
Disenchant
Plains
Island x13

